# Netlify / Vercel _headers file — applied per-path by the CDN edge.
# T-193: The /p/:slug public share page renders LLM-generated Markdown and
# is unauthenticated. A strict CSP limits what injected content can do.

/p/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; img-src 'self' data: https:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; script-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# Issue #18: public storyboards at /sb/<slug> are intentionally noindex, to
# match /p/*. Unlike /p/*, /sb/ is a client-rendered SPA route that needs its
# own JS, so it gets the noindex header WITHOUT the strict scriptless CSP.
# Document-level noindex stack: robots.txt Disallow is the primary guard for
# non-JS crawlers; this X-Robots-Tag is the secondary layer (only if the edge
# honors _headers); the JS-injected meta covers JS crawlers. (The backend
# X-Robots-Tag is on the public storyboard API JSON, not this HTML document.)
/sb/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
